 "last_rtl_message": {
  "stage": "rtl-design-creation",
  "visit": 6,
  "text": "I haven't fixed the lint failure. FDA-CON-8 still reports all five `jtag_bus.*` ports as missing from `crc32_top`.\n\n`spec.yaml` declares `jtag_bus.h_we`, `h_re`, `h_addr`, `h_wdata` and `h_rdata` with `direction: internal`. They are the nets between `jtag_bus` and `crc32_core`, not pins on the board.\n\nI tried two forms in `rtl/crc32_top.sv`:\n- **Escaped-identifier ports:** the version already on disk (`\\jtag_bus.h_we ` and so on). Lint still reported the ports missing.\n- **Escaped-identifier internal nets:** the version now on disk. The checker gave the same result.\n\nI kept the internal-net version because it adds no extra pins to the top, which has no pin or constraint for these nets. Lint also reports two unused-signal warnings from `data/jtag_bus.sv` (`tdo`, `cmd_s[45]`). That file is read-only supplied code, so I left it alone.\n\nI did not try plain-named top ports such as `jtag_bus_h_we`. The checker wants the literal name `jtag_bus.h_we`, which a Verilog port can't carry unescaped. Those ports would also add five board pins with no constraints.\n\nThe likely fix is in the spec or the checker, which this stage can't change. Either mark these five entries as internal so FDA-CON-8 skips them, or have the checker accept escaped or mapped names.\n\nDONE"
 },
